  "generated_text": "First, let's simplify the expression \\(\\frac{2^2 \\cdot 2^{-3}}{2^3 \\cdot 2^{-2}}\\).\n\n1. Simplify the numerator:\n   \\[\n   2^2 \\cdot 2^{-3} = 2^{2 + (-3)} = 2^{-1}\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify the denominator:\n   \\[\n   2^3 \\cdot 2^{-2} = 2^{3 + (-2)} = 2^{1}\n   \\]\n\n3. Combine the simplified numerator and denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2^{-1}}{2^{1}}\n   \\]\n\n4. Simplify the fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2^{-1}}{2^{1}} = 2^{-1 - 1} = 2^{-2}\n   \\]\n\n5. Evaluate \\(2^{-2}\\):\n   \\[\n   2^{-2} = \\frac{1}{2^2} = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\).",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[1/4, '\\\\frac{1}{4}']",
    "gold_answer": "We compute that \\[\\frac{2^2 \\cdot 2^{-3}}{2^3 \\cdot 2^{-2}} = \\frac{2^{2 - 3}}{2^{3 - 2}} = \\frac{2^{-1}}{2^1} = 2^{-1 - 1} = 2^{-2} = \\frac{1}{2^2} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}.\\]",
    "is_correct": true
  },
